{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507211648,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNjMxMzM4NjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1874","origin":"github"},"title":"a simple create is way too slow if invoked within a \"rich\" hierarchy","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nwhatever should take a second top, takes a minute (or even two).  Thus for 1000 datasets, I will need to wait about 16-32  hours just to get them created :-(\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\ntake some good hierarchy of directories/files (in my case a tree inbox/year/date/accession/study with bunch of DICOMs) and create a hierarchy of datasets at each of those levels, using `datalad create -d inbox $PWD/inbox/year/date/accession/study` (or at any level above) command.  I guess for sorting the paths or smth datalad does 'git diff' or 'status' which takes awhile... or may be something else. dunno yet\n\nHere is a complete script\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n\nset -eu\n\n# helper since we blow if there is already a dataset there\nfunction createds() {\n p=\"$1\"\n [ -e \"$p/.datalad\" ] || \\\n   datalad create -d inbox --force --no-annex $PWD/$p\n}\n\ndatalad create --force --no-annex inbox;\nfor yds in inbox/*; do   # year\n  createds $yds;\n  for mds in $yds/*; do   # month\n      createds $mds;\n      for dds in $mds/*; do   # day\n         createds $dds;\n         for ads in $dds/*; do   # accession\n             [ -e \"$ads/.datalad\" ] || datalad create -d inbox --force  $PWD/$ads;\n             # finally add data\n             datalad add -d $ads -m \"adding all the data\" $PWD/$ads/*;\n             # tune up configuration per @mih recommendation\n             git -C $ads config --file .datalad/config --replace-all metadata.nativetype dicom\n             git -C $ads config --file .datalad/config --replace-all metadata.aggregate-content-datalad-core no\n             git -C $ads config --file .datalad/config --replace-all metadata.store-aggregate-content no\n             # ATM can't do create with enh-metadata option, so we will do in two stages\n             # datalad aggregate-metadata -d $ads\n         done;\n      done\n   done\ndone\n```\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad plugin wtf`)?\n\n0.9.1 atm\n\nedit 1:\nyeap:\n```\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,437 [DEBUG  ] Committing via direct call of git: ['git', 'commit', '-m', '[DATALAD] new dataset']\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,438 [DEBUG  ] Running: ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'commit', '-m', '[DATALAD] new dataset', '--', '.datalad/.gitattributes', '.datalad/config']\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,482 [DEBUG  ] Running: ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'show', '--no-patch', '--format=%H', '--']\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,510 [DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.distribution.add.Add'\u003e\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,511 [DEBUG  ] Running: ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'show', '--no-patch', '--format=%H', '--']\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,539 [DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.interface.annotate_paths.AnnotatePaths'\u003e\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,540 [DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.interface.diff.Diff'\u003e\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,541 [DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.interface.annotate_paths.AnnotatePaths'\u003e\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,542 [DEBUG  ] Running: ['git', '--work-tree=.', 'diff', '--raw', '-z', '--ignore-submodules=none', '--abbrev=40', 'HEAD', '--']\n2017-10-05 13:56:58,615 [DEBUG  ] Running: ['git', '--work-tree=.', 'status', '--porcelain', '-z', '--ignore-submodules=all', '--untracked=all']\n..... LONG WAIT....\n2017-10-05 13:58:28,628 [DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.interface.diff.Diff'\u003e\n... some other stuff which takes seconds\n```\n\nand apparently I cannot provide multiple paths to the single `create` call :-/\n```\n(dev) [yoh@rolando test]$ DATALAD_LOG_TIMESTAMP=yes datalad -l debug create -d inbox --no-annex --force /mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/*\n2017-10-05 14:00:36,218 [ERROR  ] unknown arguments: ['/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/03', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/07', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/08', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/09', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/12', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/13', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/14', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/19', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/22', '/mnt/DICOM/test/inbox/2016/09/26']\n```","files":null}]}